  "details": "Version: VRCSDK2\nUnity: 2018.4.20f1\nAfter a few play tests I've noticed that the performance in Meat Grinder has decreased on both platforms, there is a stutter about every few seconds or so and it seems like the issue might be related to a NullReferenceException that happens when an object spawns. \nI'm spawning objects by having the objects in the scene and referencing them in the dynamic prefabs world descriptor and then using SpawnObject on the trigger referencing that.\nSpawning actual prefabs instead of scene objects will not trigger the error it seems like.\nThe exception in question is... about 16 642 characters long -> https://pastebin.com/yKGeYk7j\nYou can test this in Meat Grinder: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_c6b6c1fa-ed05-46eb-a148-38655c64b8e4",
